WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:33.000
This is 99% Invisible. I'm Roman Mars. In South Liverpool, there's a neighborhood called Granby. It used to be one of the most vibrant and diverse neighborhoods in the UK. It had a busy main street lined with shops and cafes. But by 2012, when an architect named Louis Jones first visited, most of the houses were unoccupied. So, you know, a couple of hundred houses, but only about 10 or 12 people still living there. the rest of the house is all empty.
这里是《99% Invisible》。我是罗曼·马斯。在利物浦南部，有一个叫格兰比的街区。它曾经是英国最具活力和多元化的街区之一。这里曾有一条挂满商店和咖啡馆的繁华主街。但到了2012年，当一位名叫路易斯·琼斯的建筑师第一次来访时，大多数房子都无人居住。你知道的，几百栋房子里只有大约10到12个人还在那里生活，其余的房子全空着。

2
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Granby had suffered through decades of unemployment, aggressive policing, and failed redevelopment schemes. And over time, the neighborhood had hollowed out. That's 99PI senior editor, Delaney Hall. The local government had forced residents to sell their homes and then boarded them up. But before the authorities sealed each house, they gutted it. They'd strip everything out.
格兰比经历了数十年的失业、强力治安和失败的重建计划。随着时间的推移，这个街区被掏空了。这是99PI的高级编辑德兰妮·霍尔。当地政府曾迫使居民卖掉房屋，然后将它们用木板封起来。但在当局封锁每栋房子之前，他们会将其内部拆空。他们会剥离掉所有东西。

3
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:21.000
They'd strip out the copper, the lead, everything that was seen to have an economic value, but also everything that would enable someone to live there, the toilets, the kind of infrastructure. And that was to prevent people from squatting in those houses after they'd been emptied out. And after stripping the houses and boarding up the windows, the government would place a sign on the front, reading.
他们会剥离铜、铅以及所有被认为具有经济价值的东西，还有所有能让人生存的东西，比如马桶和各种基础设施。这是为了防止人们在房屋被清空后非法侵占。在剥离了房屋并用木板封住窗户后，政府会在正门贴上一块牌子，上面写着。

4
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:54.000
All items of value have been removed from this property. And, you know, it's quite a provocation when every single house on the street says on it, no items of value in this house. Of course, the government meant materials like copper and lead. But there are other kinds of value embedded in a home. There's the skill it took to build it and the years of life that happened inside of it and the community that grew up around it. And what happened next in Granby would prove the signs wrong.
本物业所有有价值的物品均已被搬走。你知道的，当街上的每一栋房子都写着“此房屋内无有价物品”时，这是一种相当大的挑衅。当然，政府指的是铜和铅等材料。但房屋中还蕴含着其他价值。包括建造它所需的技能、其中度过的岁月，以及围绕它成长起来的社区。接下来在格兰比发生的事情将证明这些告示是错的。

