A small group of residents basically refused. to leave the neighborhood. Little by little, they began clearing trash from the empty lots, planting community gardens, and painting the boarded-up houses in bright colors. Eventually, this band of holdouts formed a community land trust, or a CLT. Their goal was to take ownership of the empty houses and bring people back to the neighborhood. They raised money through a patchwork of small grants, and then they realized it might be useful to have some folks on board who knew how to design and build stuff, which is how Lewis got involved.
一小群居民基本上拒绝离开这个街区。他们一点一点地开始清理空地上的垃圾、种植社区花园，并用鲜艳的颜色粉刷用木板封住的房子。最终，这群坚守者成立了一个社区土地信托，简称CLT。他们的目标是获得空置房屋的所有权，并把人们带回这个街区。他们通过零星的小额资助筹集资金，然后他们意识到，如果能有一些懂得设计和建造的人加入，可能会很有用，这就是路易斯参与进来的原因。

