most famous architecture, places like the Hyac Sophia. Notre Dame and the great mosque of Cordoba, all Guse repurposed stonework. But to really understand Spolia, you have to go back to the place where the practice first became widespread. It happened when a civilization was in the middle of an existential crisis, and it started pulling apart the old world in order to build a new one. That civilization was the Roman Empire. That's funny. I was just thinking about the Roman Empire.
