Empire. At its peak, the Roman Empire controlled the entire Mediterranean world. It spanned Europe, North Africa, and Western Asia. The empire lasted for roughly five centuries. And nearly 2,000 years later, we are still arguing about its legacy. So my name is Dr. Emma Southern. I am a Roman historian. I am an ex-academic, and now I write books about how horrible the Romans were. Emma loves to hate the Romans. She has been obsessed ever since she first learned about them as a teenager. The thing that I love the most about them more than any other empire really is the complete disconnect between their image of themselves
