as being the most rational, the most perfect, the peak of civilization, the best that humanity can be, combined with the actual reality of what their empire was, which was a horrifically violent machine, that chewed up land, it chewed up resources, and produced marble buildings and emperors. The Romans projected power through architecture. Emperors built enormous monuments to prove that they were rich and legitimate. Emperor Augustus famously claimed that he, quote, found Rome a city of brick and left it a city of marble. Hadrian built the pantheon. Trajan built his famous column. The Flavian emperors made the
认为自己是最理性、最完美、文明的顶峰、人类所能成为的最好状态，而这与他们的帝国的真实现实之间存在着彻底的脱节——那是一个极其暴力的机器，它吞噬土地、吞噬资源，并制造出大理石建筑和皇帝。罗马人通过建筑投射权力。皇帝们建造巨大的纪念碑来证明他们富有且合法。奥古斯都皇帝曾有一句名言，称他“发现了一个砖砌的罗马，却留下了一个大理石的罗马”。哈德良建造了万神殿。图拉真建造了他著名的圆柱。弗拉维王朝的皇帝们建造了

