These Roman quarries were state-owned and they relied mostly on slave labor. They were located in hot, dry places and they were all overseen by the army. It was terrible backbreaking work. After mining the marble, the Romans shipped it across the Mediterranean and used it to build the kind of magnificent structures they became famous for. And that's how it went for many centuries. The Romans built monuments to show how awesome they were, using rare stone from far-flung places, and the message it conveyed was clear. Rome was eternal.
这些罗马采石场属于国有，主要依靠奴隶劳动力。它们位于炎热干燥的地方，全部由军队监督。这是可怕的、累垮人的工作。开采大理石后，罗马人将其通过地中海运送，并用它来建造使他们闻名遐迩的宏伟建筑。几个世纪以来一直如此。罗马人建造纪念碑来展示他们的伟大，使用的是来自遥远地方的稀有石头，传达的信息很明确：罗马是永恒的。

